From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:52:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(task): build the end-of-task report with a verdict that
 cannot be talked up

Sixth slice: the report the task document requires at the end of every task,
and the separation between "the state machine got here" and "and this is what
that proves".

core/task/TaskReport.kt:
- TaskVerdict is VERIFIED only when the task finished AND every required check
  ran and passed. Finished-looking states without checks are NOT_VERIFIED, a
  failed step or check is FAILED, and a declined or refused task is CANCELLED.
  Each of those adds a ReportCaveat that the report renders under
  "not verified", so "no checks were run" can never be shown as success.
- TaskReport carries request, per-step records (state, paths, failure,
  attempts), checks with their classification and one-line evidence, the policy
  decisions from the audit log, recorded memory fact ids, limitations,
  needsNewApk and duration - all observed facts, no prose from a model.
- render() is a convenience text view for a PR body or a bug report.
- TaskStep gains `failure`, so a failed step explains itself in the trail.

Tests: TaskReportBuilderTest (13), including that every success state counts
only with green checks and that an environment-blocked check is not reported as
broken code.
